      en: "Thubursicum Numidarum is an ancient Roman city located in Souk Ahras Province, northeastern Algeria, near the Tunisian border. Founded in the 1st century AD, it prospered under Numidian and Roman rule. The ruins include a forum, theater, temples, and baths. The city was a center for grain production and trade. It was destroyed by Vandals in the 5th century, later rebuilt by Byzantines, and eventually abandoned. Excavations have revealed mosaics, statues, and inscriptions. The site has been protected since 1982.",
